WEBVTT

00:11.800 --> 00:15.849
The Abyss Gate in Achromatic Darkness
that your party sealed is open.

00:15.850 --> 00:18.360
So the seal has been undone?

00:18.630 --> 00:22.860
And the darkness flowing in through it is
pouring out through every other dungeon.

00:23.080 --> 00:26.559
We need to conquer Achromatic
Darkness and close the Abyss Gate.

00:26.560 --> 00:30.329
Then the influx of darkness and its
outflow into other dungeons will stop,

00:30.330 --> 00:32.000
and the world will be saved.

00:34.750 --> 00:38.340
Let's hurry back to Finis—
to Achromatic Darkness!

00:47.140 --> 00:54.100
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:09.010 --> 02:09.849
(Episode 21: Tenebre)

02:09.850 --> 02:12.709
(Episode 21: Tenebre)
Wait. If you're talking
about closing an Abyss Gate,

02:12.710 --> 02:15.010
(Episode 21: Tenebre)
we're going to need a special investigation.

02:15.560 --> 02:19.879
And moving through a dungeon that dangerous
while protecting the investigation team

02:19.880 --> 02:21.520
might as well be impossible.

02:22.000 --> 02:24.400
Then we won't take them with us.

02:24.770 --> 02:27.030
We're not going to close it.
We're going to destroy it.

02:27.330 --> 02:29.909
We tried that, too.

02:29.910 --> 02:32.729
But no matter what we did,
it wouldn't break.

02:32.730 --> 02:34.530
That's why we sealed it.

02:42.440 --> 02:46.680
This is also top-secret, so it's
not in the official records.

02:47.800 --> 02:52.219
That said, I'm now starting to
see how we can save this world.

02:52.220 --> 02:54.439
I'll send a letter to Beecha.

02:54.440 --> 02:55.470
Right.

02:55.820 --> 03:00.379
He'll need to send Forneia for us if
we're going back to Finis, anyway.

03:00.380 --> 03:04.480
I'd like to have him put out another
royal order to gather A-rank adventurers.

03:05.320 --> 03:09.739
We'll also need an advance investigation
to see what's going on

03:09.740 --> 03:11.569
inside Achromatic Darkness right now.

03:11.570 --> 03:14.989
How long will it take before
you can return to Finis?

03:14.990 --> 03:19.750
Well, there's sending the letter, getting
permission, preparing, and the round trip...

03:20.200 --> 03:22.250
I'd say it'll take at least two weeks.

03:22.550 --> 03:24.499
We can't wait that long!

03:24.500 --> 03:26.859
Isn't there some way... some way to...

03:26.860 --> 03:28.760
Yuke, you should call it a day.

03:29.080 --> 03:30.259
This is not the time to—

03:30.260 --> 03:31.509
No.

03:31.510 --> 03:33.829
That's an order from your guild master.

03:33.830 --> 03:37.349
Rest. You haven't slept
at all since yesterday.

03:37.350 --> 03:40.800
Get plenty of rest, and then we'll
think about this. All right?

03:44.420 --> 03:47.279
Benwood is right, you know.

03:47.280 --> 03:49.320
Let's get some rest, okay?

03:50.020 --> 03:50.890
Rune...

03:51.620 --> 03:53.959
You ought to listen to her.

03:53.960 --> 03:56.079
Haven't you heard the saying?

03:56.080 --> 03:59.830
"Haste makes waste.
Slow and steady wins the race."

04:00.350 --> 04:02.580
This is precisely the time
when you need to remain calm.

04:02.880 --> 04:04.460
I will retire, as well.

04:06.510 --> 04:08.460
All right. I'll rest.

04:09.090 --> 04:11.029
Let's head back, Rune.

04:11.030 --> 04:11.960
Yeah!

04:22.080 --> 04:26.019
You mean all dungeons in the world
are connected to Achromatic Darkness?

04:26.020 --> 04:29.230
Yes. All dungeons are connected as one.

04:34.870 --> 04:37.740
That's right... They're all connected!

04:51.320 --> 04:53.649
If you felt the need to wake me up,

04:53.650 --> 04:55.880
does that mean you came up
with some brilliant idea?

04:56.230 --> 04:58.859
You see? Resting truly is important.

04:58.860 --> 05:00.400
We won't go back to Finis.

05:01.600 --> 05:03.860
All dungeons are connected.

05:04.360 --> 05:08.020
That means we can get to Achromatic
Darkness through the royal mausoleum.

05:08.340 --> 05:12.280
Did you not suffer enough
the first time, Warlock?

05:13.970 --> 05:16.689
Still, I understand what you're saying.

05:16.690 --> 05:19.530
You'll have the Seeker's
Compass to guide you.

05:21.410 --> 05:23.330
How good are the chances?

05:23.830 --> 05:25.609
I think it'll be fifty-fifty.

05:25.610 --> 05:28.420
So I'm going to go inside alone.

05:28.870 --> 05:31.670
Alone? Isn't that dangerous?

05:32.490 --> 05:34.199
The truth is...

05:34.200 --> 05:36.800
I've received the blessing of
an evil god from another world.

05:38.770 --> 05:41.300
You have? This is news to me.

05:41.890 --> 05:44.739
It's not something I go
around telling everyone.

05:44.740 --> 05:46.060
Only friends need to know.

05:47.000 --> 05:50.959
I don't know if that god has any
connection to Achromatic Darkness,

05:50.960 --> 05:53.040
but I have ties to that place.

05:53.580 --> 05:56.239
So all I need is the Seeker's Compass.

05:56.240 --> 05:57.679
Good grief.

05:57.680 --> 06:01.490
This sounds very well planned
for a fifty-fifty chance.

06:02.590 --> 06:06.789
Yuke, I would like to throw
my support behind your plan.

06:06.790 --> 06:08.750
It probably has the best odds of working.

06:09.080 --> 06:10.289
I'll lend you the compass.

06:10.290 --> 06:11.429
Really?

06:11.430 --> 06:13.360
But first...

06:14.300 --> 06:16.510
You should consult with your wives.

06:17.810 --> 06:20.039
Warlock and hero,

06:20.040 --> 06:22.399
if you intend to risk your life,

06:22.400 --> 06:26.020
you must not neglect those
who are bound to your life.

06:26.500 --> 06:29.829
In the same way that you are prepared
to risk your life for this mission,

06:29.830 --> 06:33.780
there are those who would risk
their lives to stay by your side.

06:35.590 --> 06:37.900
Like your child bride there.

06:38.410 --> 06:40.280
I'm not a child bride.

06:40.830 --> 06:41.910
Right. Of course not.

06:42.210 --> 06:44.209
H-How long have you been there?

06:44.210 --> 06:45.540
A little while now.

06:46.040 --> 06:48.290
A-Are you... angry?

06:50.850 --> 06:52.540
Thanks, Your Highness.

06:52.860 --> 06:56.299
Oh, I was just taking my
meddling a bit too far.

06:56.300 --> 07:00.269
No, Yuke doesn't have many
friends, so he needed it.

07:00.270 --> 07:02.679
You can expect a lecture later.

07:02.680 --> 07:03.759
Right...

07:03.760 --> 07:07.079
You have excellent wives
who understand you well.

07:07.080 --> 07:08.770
Talk to them.

07:09.080 --> 07:11.079
I'll do that.

07:11.080 --> 07:12.770
Thanks, Mastoma.

07:13.200 --> 07:16.320
My friend,
I have no desire to see you die.

07:16.920 --> 07:19.530
That said, there is a time when
it is right to risk it all.

07:20.110 --> 07:23.530
If you must go, I'll
steel my resolve, as well.

07:24.110 --> 07:24.820
Okay.

07:33.090 --> 07:33.780
Hmph.

07:35.960 --> 07:38.170
Um, so...

07:39.240 --> 07:40.170
Rain?

07:40.790 --> 07:41.540
Hmph.

07:49.380 --> 07:50.810
Sorry, Rain.

07:52.040 --> 07:52.900
Okay.

07:58.190 --> 08:00.070
What's this about, Yuke?

08:00.850 --> 08:05.789
When I thought about how
I might die, I got scared...

08:05.790 --> 08:07.530
and I wanted to touch you.

08:08.140 --> 08:09.330
Does it bother you?

08:09.840 --> 08:12.170
No, it doesn't bother me.

08:26.660 --> 08:27.430
What's wrong?

08:27.890 --> 08:28.980
I felt something...

08:30.170 --> 08:32.809
That's not what I meant!

08:32.810 --> 08:34.289
What, then?

08:34.290 --> 08:35.230
I think...

08:35.870 --> 08:37.930
it was the same thing you have here.

08:41.000 --> 08:42.240
So that's the story.

08:42.560 --> 08:43.600
What do you think?

08:45.780 --> 08:48.539
Thank you for telling us about this.

08:48.540 --> 08:51.629
But you're taking too much
upon yourself, Master.

08:51.630 --> 08:52.950
Like you always do.

08:53.790 --> 08:54.960
Sorry.

08:55.240 --> 08:57.069
I understand how you feel.

08:57.070 --> 08:59.989
We're all rather
disturbed by this, as well.

08:59.990 --> 09:01.710
But there's nothing to think about!

09:02.100 --> 09:04.029
I'm going with you!

09:04.030 --> 09:05.029
Marina...

09:05.030 --> 09:06.849
Naturally, I will, as well.

09:06.850 --> 09:08.970
I won't be slowing you down.

09:09.660 --> 09:12.939
You should know better than
any of us how crazy it is

09:12.940 --> 09:15.600
to go into Achromatic
Darkness without a scout!

09:16.510 --> 09:17.350
I'll go, too!

09:17.870 --> 09:19.610
We're going with you this time.

09:21.520 --> 09:22.609
Guys, listen...

09:22.610 --> 09:24.469
Nope! Not listening!

09:24.470 --> 09:26.569
You're going to tell us
we can't this time, right?

09:26.570 --> 09:28.359
We're not gonna listen to that!

09:28.360 --> 09:29.200
But...

09:29.550 --> 09:31.179
No buts allowed!

09:31.180 --> 09:32.540
We're going and that's that!

09:32.990 --> 09:36.540
Master, I can't have
you taking us lightly.

09:36.840 --> 09:38.649
I'm not taking you lightly.

09:38.650 --> 09:41.629
You've all become
genuinely good adventurers.

09:41.630 --> 09:45.269
That's right. We're adventurers now.

09:45.270 --> 09:47.629
We're not your students anymore.

09:47.630 --> 09:50.109
Master... no, Yuke.

09:50.110 --> 09:52.750
We go where you go. No matter what.

09:53.760 --> 09:57.220
Just give up already.
We've made up our minds.

09:58.790 --> 10:00.270
Okay. I understand.

10:00.570 --> 10:01.150
Yeah!

10:01.480 --> 10:02.150
Yes!

10:02.510 --> 10:03.230
Jeez...

10:03.540 --> 10:04.150
Right!

10:05.280 --> 10:07.199
Don't you have anything to say, Rain?

10:07.200 --> 10:07.900
Me?

10:08.460 --> 10:10.909
I've already told him how I feel.

10:10.910 --> 10:12.239
You did? When?!

10:12.240 --> 10:13.030
No fair!

10:15.300 --> 10:18.500
In that case, Yuke, please
explain the plan to us.

10:18.950 --> 10:20.900
We'll use the Seeker's Compass.

10:22.060 --> 10:25.759
Achromatic Darkness is connected
to all other dungeons.

10:25.760 --> 10:26.260
So...

10:26.800 --> 10:30.260
You mean we're going into
Tenebre in the royal mausoleum?

10:31.020 --> 10:32.510
Yes, that's right.

10:32.790 --> 10:36.539
We're certain it's connected
to Achromatic Darkness.

10:36.540 --> 10:38.559
We'll use the Seeker's Compass

10:38.560 --> 10:41.520
to find a route to Achromatic
Darkness and the Abyss Gate.

10:42.060 --> 10:46.030
All right. I'll figure out
what supplies we need.

10:46.330 --> 10:49.539
I'll also work out
our schedule for going in.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.799
We'll want the guild's support, too.

10:51.800 --> 10:55.030
I'll put together a plan and
then run it by the guild.

10:55.320 --> 10:57.500
A-All right. Please do.

10:57.800 --> 10:59.999
Just leave it to us, Yuke.

11:00.000 --> 11:03.000
If anyone can do this, it's us. Right?

11:03.320 --> 11:04.060
Right!

11:05.080 --> 11:07.210
I beg your pardon, Lord Feldio!

11:07.540 --> 11:12.260
Prince Mastoma urgently requests your
presence at the Adventurer's Guild.

11:15.540 --> 11:17.769
Prince Rafuma is on the move?!

11:17.770 --> 11:19.359
To the royal mausoleum, yes.

11:19.360 --> 11:22.770
"It's just a monster nest," he said.
"I'll stomp it out."

11:23.300 --> 11:26.399
He came all the way to my mansion
to say that, and then he was gone.

11:26.400 --> 11:30.009
The streaming relay devices
are ready to operate.

11:30.010 --> 11:31.150
Beta, turn them on.

11:37.920 --> 11:39.139
Signal received.

11:39.140 --> 11:40.410
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

11:40.950 --> 11:43.170
And for my foolish brother.

11:43.690 --> 11:44.590
Found him.

11:45.330 --> 11:45.920
But...

11:49.140 --> 11:51.209
Well, he's doomed.

11:51.210 --> 11:52.840
What should we do? Rescue them?

11:53.180 --> 11:55.749
We'd never get there in time.

11:55.750 --> 11:57.349
That idiot!

11:57.350 --> 11:58.990
Viscount, over there!

12:01.580 --> 12:03.730
He's abandoning his soldiers
and fleeing alone?!

12:04.060 --> 12:05.520
How despicable.

12:08.570 --> 12:10.610
I've lost sight of Prince Rafuma.

12:10.930 --> 12:14.279
He may have left the streaming range.

12:14.280 --> 12:15.160
I'll search for him.

12:15.750 --> 12:16.889
What do we do?

12:16.890 --> 12:19.450
We will need to bolster our security.

12:19.720 --> 12:22.019
Once those monsters develop
a taste for people,

12:22.020 --> 12:24.710
they may head toward Ra-jo.

12:25.290 --> 12:26.809
That's true.

12:26.810 --> 12:28.710
I guess we'll have to make our move.

12:29.840 --> 12:31.159
To Tenebre?!

12:31.160 --> 12:32.840
And I think we should hurry.

12:33.130 --> 12:37.389
I thought it would be wise to come
up with a plan before leaving, but...

12:37.390 --> 12:39.970
We don't have that luxury anymore.

12:41.010 --> 12:42.269
Can you do this?

12:42.270 --> 12:43.439
How should I know?

12:43.440 --> 12:44.460
I've found him.

12:47.600 --> 12:48.230
Damn it!

12:52.740 --> 12:55.369
He just touched Tenebre!

12:55.370 --> 12:56.070
Yeah.

13:00.600 --> 13:02.080
A Shadow Stalker?!

13:11.840 --> 13:13.639
What on earth was that?

13:13.640 --> 13:15.470
A Shadow Stalker.

13:15.970 --> 13:18.830
A mysterious being that
appears in dungeons...

13:19.480 --> 13:24.100
but it looks like we've just
discovered what they are.

13:24.620 --> 13:27.989
Humans turned inside-out
by touching Tenebre...

13:27.990 --> 13:32.360
This won't work! I can't take
you guys to a place like that!

13:33.720 --> 13:35.240
Yuke...

13:40.240 --> 13:42.490
Wow, it sure is gloomy in here.

13:43.020 --> 13:44.500
Mind if I come in?

13:46.090 --> 13:46.619
Yuke, why the long face when we
haven't seen each other in so long?

13:46.620 --> 13:49.500
(Saga Feldio)
Yuke, why the long face when we
haven't seen each other in so long?

13:49.790 --> 13:51.529
U-Uncle?

13:51.530 --> 13:54.260
Your uncle? I believe it was... Saga?

13:54.630 --> 13:58.340
You've sure gotten bigger.
More dependable-looking, too.

13:58.890 --> 14:01.720
You have the face of a great adventurer.

14:02.130 --> 14:05.169
Why are you here?! I mean, where
have you been all this time?!

14:05.170 --> 14:10.309
Saga! You dumped everything on us and
took off! Where the hell were you?!

14:10.310 --> 14:11.860
We can talk about that later.

14:12.360 --> 14:16.990
I'm surprised to see my simple-minded,
late-blooming Yuke sitting by such a beauty.

14:17.530 --> 14:18.990
U-Um...

14:19.410 --> 14:22.419
What do you think of Yuke, Miss?

14:22.420 --> 14:23.870
Is he taking care of you?

14:24.220 --> 14:27.370
Y-Yuke treats me very well.

14:27.670 --> 14:28.750
Uncle!

14:29.060 --> 14:30.849
All right, good!

14:30.850 --> 14:33.609
You guys are all a bit too tense.

14:33.610 --> 14:35.750
We can't have a calm conversation
this way.

14:36.080 --> 14:38.510
Indeed. And who might you be?

14:38.840 --> 14:40.539
I'm Saga Feldio,

14:40.540 --> 14:43.140
a humble adventurer and his uncle.

14:43.690 --> 14:44.969
Is that so?

14:44.970 --> 14:49.770
I am Mastoma, Yuke's friend and
leader of this town, Ra-jo.

14:50.110 --> 14:53.959
I'm so glad Yuke has a friend like you.

14:53.960 --> 14:54.770
Saga!

14:55.150 --> 15:00.349
It's because you left that a careless
guy like me ended up guild master!

15:00.350 --> 15:03.349
Sorry about that.
I had some things going on.

15:03.350 --> 15:05.030
Still, you have Mamar, don't you?

15:05.480 --> 15:08.370
And I did come back, just like I promised.

15:09.200 --> 15:10.410
To stop that.

15:10.990 --> 15:15.019
You're as full of confidence as ever.

15:15.020 --> 15:16.670
Can you even do anything about this?

15:17.000 --> 15:18.360
Of course not.

15:18.810 --> 15:20.159
At least, not alone.

15:20.160 --> 15:21.430
Me?!

15:22.500 --> 15:26.179
You're an A-rank adventurer,
a dungeon count, and a hero?

15:26.180 --> 15:28.680
My puny little nephew?

15:30.020 --> 15:34.379
Well? The neat and tidy Silk,
the energetic Marina,

15:34.380 --> 15:37.190
the wild Nene, or the witch Jamie?

15:37.590 --> 15:38.940
Which one are you after?

15:39.240 --> 15:41.700
Cut it out! It's not like that!

15:42.040 --> 15:44.759
Don't tell me
it's the young-looking Niberune.

15:44.760 --> 15:47.509
Young-looking? What are you
talking about? She is young!

15:47.510 --> 15:50.700
You know, that's a crime in Welmelia...
or anywhere, really.

15:51.030 --> 15:52.740
I'd obviously never mess with her!

15:53.870 --> 15:55.960
Then have you messed with Rain?

15:56.930 --> 15:58.449
A young thing like her?

15:58.450 --> 16:00.460
R-Rain is older than me!

16:00.820 --> 16:02.009
Really?

16:02.010 --> 16:03.649
Only by a few months...

16:03.650 --> 16:05.409
Wait, what do you mean, "messed with" her?

16:05.410 --> 16:07.470
How did you know... wait, no!

16:08.280 --> 16:10.309
You had the Stigmata on you.

16:10.310 --> 16:14.480
Ordinary people probably
couldn't tell, but I can.

16:14.890 --> 16:16.110
Stigmata?

16:16.540 --> 16:20.730
Yeah. Put simply, it's an element
in giving up one's humanity.

16:21.530 --> 16:23.990
Oh, Persephone's mark...

16:24.290 --> 16:28.019
You got that from the Pale,
Immortal Ruler?

16:28.020 --> 16:29.120
Well, damn.

16:29.400 --> 16:32.130
I got it the last time I went
into Achromatic Darkness.

16:32.680 --> 16:39.130
That's basically proof of your
identity in worlds other than this one.

16:39.670 --> 16:41.130
Proof?

16:43.760 --> 16:47.530
Rune was safe thanks to Loge's protection,

16:48.250 --> 16:51.329
but I was safe thanks to the Stigmata.

16:51.330 --> 16:52.770
Is that what you're saying?

16:53.090 --> 16:56.859
I could sense the same
kind of thing on Rain.

16:56.860 --> 16:58.829
You gave it to her, right?

16:58.830 --> 16:59.900
I did?

17:09.300 --> 17:10.230
That's when...

17:12.310 --> 17:15.179
So if we received the Stigmata from Yuke,

17:15.180 --> 17:18.250
we would also be unaffected by Tenebre?

17:18.570 --> 17:20.039
You understood right.

17:20.040 --> 17:23.760
In that case, Yuke, please
give us the Stigmata.

17:24.070 --> 17:25.329
H-Hey...

17:25.330 --> 17:26.760
We've told you over and over again!

17:27.050 --> 17:28.809
We won't let you go alone!

17:28.810 --> 17:32.769
You called us your family,
so we're with you until the end!

17:32.770 --> 17:33.369
Me, too!

17:33.370 --> 17:34.179
Same goes for me!

17:34.180 --> 17:34.770
And me.

17:35.560 --> 17:37.270
You're sure about this?

17:37.530 --> 17:40.029
This might make me a little bit jealous...

17:40.030 --> 17:41.900
But I'll close my eyes.

17:43.190 --> 17:46.469
Young ladies, have you
thought this through?

17:46.470 --> 17:48.910
You might never be able to come back.

17:49.220 --> 17:53.580
Did you know seven-leaf clovers
hold endless good fortune?

17:53.880 --> 17:56.239
We trust Yuke.

17:56.240 --> 17:58.830
No matter what happens,
we won't be left unhappy.

18:04.060 --> 18:05.460
Seven-leaf, eh?

18:06.090 --> 18:10.349
Good grief. My stubborn nephew's
girlfriends are all as stubborn as he is.

18:10.350 --> 18:11.559
They're not my—

18:11.560 --> 18:13.970
Do as you will, as long as you're
prepared for what it means.

18:14.610 --> 18:18.270
You're all full-fledged
adventurers now, after all.

18:18.980 --> 18:21.480
(A Few Days Later)

18:25.280 --> 18:28.789
Did you give the Stigmata
to everyone in Clover?

18:28.790 --> 18:33.410
Well... I can't let them
turn into Shadow Stalkers.

18:33.740 --> 18:37.160
Of course, Rune doesn't need it,
so I didn't do anything to her.

18:37.490 --> 18:40.190
I won't ask how you did it.

18:41.700 --> 18:44.849
Per the plan, I'll head to Finis now

18:44.850 --> 18:46.789
and enter Achromatic Darkness.

18:46.790 --> 18:48.420
Me and Benwood.

18:48.930 --> 18:50.589
I have to ask...

18:50.590 --> 18:54.049
This teleportation artifact
you're using to get to Finis

18:54.050 --> 18:57.349
can't take us along with you?

18:57.350 --> 18:59.589
Unfortunately, it only seats two.

18:59.590 --> 19:00.560
Oh, okay.

19:01.390 --> 19:05.730
Yuke, I'm sorry to
force this job onto you.

19:06.420 --> 19:09.320
All I want you to do is live a happy life.

19:09.660 --> 19:11.519
You're not forcing anything on me.

19:11.520 --> 19:13.570
This is our world we're talking about.

19:14.130 --> 19:17.870
I want to tell you that there's really
no need for you to sacrifice yourself.

19:18.730 --> 19:20.450
But... I'm counting on you.

19:22.210 --> 19:23.960
Yes, Teacher!

19:25.630 --> 19:27.590
Haven't been called that in a while.

19:28.280 --> 19:31.650
You were the one who showed
me the path of the adventurer.

19:32.290 --> 19:36.100
You're always showing me
the way, even now.

19:36.420 --> 19:38.389
You can't keep saying that.

19:38.390 --> 19:42.399
You have your own companions that
you need to show the way to now.

19:42.400 --> 19:43.719
I know.

19:43.720 --> 19:44.730
Then we're all good.

19:45.190 --> 19:48.590
Let's do this, Yuke. Let's save our world.

19:49.160 --> 19:51.860
See you at the Abyss Gate.

19:55.950 --> 19:57.709
I'm counting on you, Yuke.

19:57.710 --> 19:59.870
And I'm trusting you to evacuate Ra-jo.

20:02.150 --> 20:04.319
You remember how to use it, right?

20:04.320 --> 20:06.000
Yeah, no problem.

20:06.590 --> 20:09.550
Sorry to do this in front
of you, Yuke. Forgive me.

20:12.540 --> 20:14.819
Thanks for everything, Your Highness.

20:14.820 --> 20:16.739
Be careful out there.

20:16.740 --> 20:18.260
Keep Yuke safe.

20:19.560 --> 20:20.959
And make sure you return.

20:20.960 --> 20:23.239
I will. We'll have tea together again.

20:23.240 --> 20:24.270
With Lady Mejarna, too.

20:26.080 --> 20:30.029
I will oversee Clover's
livestream personally.

20:30.030 --> 20:32.400
That's very reassuring, Viscount.

20:32.720 --> 20:35.100
I will fulfill my duty, as well.

20:35.720 --> 20:36.620
I wish you luck.

20:36.930 --> 20:39.120
Thank you. I'll be back.

20:51.720 --> 20:54.009
Okay, is everyone ready?

20:54.010 --> 20:56.760
No problem! Let's do this thing!

20:57.070 --> 20:59.510
All ready. You can count on us!

21:00.080 --> 21:02.640
Leave the advance guard to me!

21:02.950 --> 21:06.310
I'll try not to slow you down this time.

21:06.690 --> 21:08.060
I'll do my best, too!

21:08.350 --> 21:10.820
Yeah. I'm with you to the end.

21:11.380 --> 21:14.820
Begin streaming!

21:15.220 --> 21:16.820
All right, it's time to go.

21:17.290 --> 21:19.589
Our destination is the end of the world.

21:19.590 --> 21:20.830
Let's have fun, but be careful.

21:21.400 --> 21:24.330
Let's go, seven-leaf Clover!

22:55.960 --> 22:56.959
(An Unexpected Reunion)

22:56.960 --> 22:59.369
(An Unexpected Reunion)
Next time, "An Unexpected Reunion."

22:59.370 --> 23:00.970
(An Unexpected Reunion)
